Description: Implements bgnorm, a generative statistical framework for
    background correction, normalisation, and quality control in multiplex
    spatial proteomics. The method models fluorescence pixel intensities as a
    three-component mixture of log-normal convolutions representing
    background, non-specific binding, and biological signal. A
    deconvolution step separates the signal component from background
    sources, and a model-based quantile normalisation (bgnormQ) unifies
    measurements across markers, samples, and three-dimensional tissue
    slices. A Jensen-Shannon Divergence metric provides automated quality
    control. A Java-free reader for Akoya PhenoCycler-Fusion QPTIFF,
    OME-TIFF, and OME-Zarr (OME-NGFF) images is included.
